  "final_message": "The root cause is in `mrr` in `billing/reports.py`. It subtracted each subscription's monthly amount from the running total instead of adding it. So the two example customers gave 0 \u2212 3000 \u2212 1000 = \u22124000 cents (\u221240.00 USD) rather than +4000.\n\n**Fix:** changed `-` to `+` in `mrr` (`billing/reports.py`, line 46). The per-subscription normalisation in `monthly_amount` was already correct: a yearly 120.00 price comes out as 10.00 per month.\n\n**Test:** added `tests/test_reports.py`, which covers a 30.00 monthly subscription plus a 120.00 yearly one and expects `{\"usd\": 4000}`. No existing test covered `mrr`. The suite passes: 25 passed.\n\n**Answer file:** wrote `answer.json` in the repo root with `{\"file\": \"reports.py\", \"function\": \"mrr\"}`. It is git-ignored by the repo's `.gitignore`, so it won't show in `git status`. I did not commit anything.",
